{
  "sourceId": "JZ-MOCK-C-P2-Q03",
  "source": "<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://jzmaths.com/papers/jz_mocks/jz_mock_c_p2_question.pdf#page=4\">JZ Mock C · Paper 2 · Question 3</a> · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://jzmaths.com/papers/jz_mocks/jz_mock_c_p2_solution.pdf#page=5\">Publisher worked answer</a>",
  "label": "JZ Mock C · Paper 2 · Question 3",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"JZ Mock C · Paper 2 · Question 3: Use a known trigonometric sum to find a symmetric cube sum. Complete question and all answer choices.\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E",
    "F"
  ],
  "correct": "E",
  "conceptIds": [
    "p1-b1-l16",
    "p1-b1-l01"
  ],
  "knowledgePattern": "Use a known trigonometric sum to find a symmetric cube sum",
  "knowledgeTags": [
    "trigonometry"
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. Squaring the sum gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Expand <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Consequently <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>. Answer E.</p>",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Find the product",
      "body": "<p>Square <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>. Expand the square and use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Keep the mixed term when expanding the square of a sum.",
      "pitfall": "The mixed term is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> when both trigonometric functions occur."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Expand the cube of the sum",
      "body": "<p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>. Expand <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, then take out a common factor from its two mixed terms.</p>",
      "recap": "Collecting a common factor lets you use a known sum and product.",
      "pitfall": "Do not replace <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Rearrange for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math> and substitute the sum and product you know.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l01",
          "reminder": "Collecting a common factor lets you use a known sum and product."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
